    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d60">

                <pb facs="0066" n="52" sameAs="frus:frus1947v06/pg52"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851G.00/1–347: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in France
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-01-03T19:00:00-05:00">January 3, 1947—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>21. <hi rendition="#italic">Newsweek</hi> Jan 6 stated that though news not yet
                    announced, US has already taken steps halt fighting Indochina and that last week
                        Bonnet<anchor n="8" xml:id="d60-f1"/> was called in by Dept and told that
                    (1) Indochinese <pb facs="0067" n="53" xml:id="pg53"/> settlement imperative,
                    (2) affair could be brought up UN any time by any power and that US would not
                    necessarily support France, (3) that US wishes ensure no lend-lease weapons
                    being used suppress Vietnam and suspects they are being used, and (4)
                        Moffat<anchor n="9" xml:id="d60-f2"/> is in area and would be glad assist
                    both sides.</p>
                <p>For your info, of four numbered statements,
                    three and one-half completely false. Only element truth was fact ActSecy
                    suggested dispute might be brought up UN by third power.</p>
                <p>Dept replying press queries that ActSecy discussed Indochina with Bonnet Dec 23
                        (Deptel 6586 Dec 24<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d60-f3"/>). Tenor his remarks made public press conf Dec 27. (Radio
                    bulletin No. 309). To this Dept has nothing add except statement <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Newsweek</hi> story pure specimen think-piece. You may
                    make similar reply queries.</p>
                <p>Sent Paris 21. Repeated Saigon 1.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
